2017 · In this world historical sense, the Russian Revolution produced Stalin and Stalinism, defeated the armies of Hitler on Soviet soil, and helped ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.smu.edu/news/archives/2017/russian-revolution-09feb2017\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"54\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Soviet Economic Growth: 1928-1 985 - DTIC\",\"description\":\"Sections V and VI discuss the elements of the Soviet system, its growth strategy, and the major economic policies that determine its growth patterns. The ...\",\"url\":\"https://apps.dtic.mil/sti/pdfs/ADA220336.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"55\",\"title\":\"2. Direct Famine Losses in Ukraine by Region in 1932, per 1000\",\"description\":\"The total number of 1932-1934 famine losses in Soviet Ukraine is estimated at 4.5 million, with 3.9 million direct losses (excess deaths) and 0.6 million ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.gis.huri.harvard.edu/media-gallery/detail/1381000/1082128\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"56\",\"title\":\"On Holodomor Loss Numbers - Holodomor 1932-33\",\"description\":\"Sep 17, 2021 · Four to five million died, roughly 15 percent of Soviet Ukraine's 30 million inhabitants. Even Mao's 1958–62 Great Leap Forward famine, ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://holodomorct.org/2021/09/17/on-holodomor-loss-numbers-2/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"57\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Was Stalin Necessary for Russia's Economic Development?\",\"description\":\"Under a variety of alternative assumptions, we find big short run costs and moderate long run gains from Stalin's economic policies. Finally, we provide three ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w19425/w19425.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"58\",\"title\":\"The Soviet economy, 1917-1991: Its life and afterlife | CEPR\",\"description\":\"Nov 7, 2017 · Russia's Soviet era was distinguished not by economic growth or human development, but by the use of the economy to build national power.\",\"url\":\"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/sovie