ica\",\"description\":\"An economic slowdown was accompanied by increased defense spending and the disastrous decision to intervene in Afghanistan in December 1979. By the time of ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/place/Soviet-Union/The-Brezhnev-era\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"71\",\"title\":\"The Collapse of the Soviet Union - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"The unsuccessful August 1991 coup against Gorbachev sealed the fate of the Soviet Union. Planned by hard-line Communists, the coup diminished Gorbachev's power ...\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1989-1992/collapse-soviet-union\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"72\",\"title\":\"Why Did the Soviet Union Collapse? - Britannica\",\"description\":\"Political policies, economics, defense spending, and the Chernobyl nuclear disaster, among other factors, contributed to the collapse of the Soviet Union in ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/story/why-did-the-soviet-union-collapse\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"73\",\"title\":\"The End of Communism and the Fate of Eastern Europe | Origins\",\"description\":\"Dec 3, 2009 · The new regimes worked to abolish capitalism and private property by nationalizing and directing all industry, agriculture, and trade. They ...Missing:  effects | Show results with:effects\",\"url\":\"https://origins.osu.edu/article/1989-twenty-years-end-communism-and-fate-eastern-europe\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"74\",\"title\":\"How the Fall of Communism in 1989 Reshaped Eastern Europe\",\"description\":\"Nov 8, 2019 · The economic turmoil following the revolutions in Central and Eastern Europe laid the groundwork for today's perceptions of democracy and capitalism.\",\"url\":\"https://www.usnews.com/news/best-countries/articles/2019-11-08/how-the-fall-of-communism-in-1989-reshaped-eastern-europe\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"75\",\"title\":\"China - Economic Reforms, Marketization, Privatization - Britannica\",\"description\":\"Thus, rural patterns of work, land leasing, and wealth changed markedly after 1978. Exceptionally good weather during the early 1980s contributed to record ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/place/China/Economic-policy-changes\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"76\",\"title\":\"China's Post-1978 Economic Development and Entry into the Global ...\",\"description\":\"Oct 10, 2023 · The reform movement began with actions by farmers to gain rights to collectively owned land and to sell excess produce in the private markets.\",\"url\":\"https://www.cato.org/publications/chinas-post-1978-economic-development-entry-global-trading-system\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"77\",\"title\":\"Deng Xiaoping and the Economic Reform | World History\",\"description\":\"The rise of Deng Xiaoping to power after Mao's death resulted in far-reaching market economy reforms and China opening up to the global trade while maintaining ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/suny-worldhistory/chapter/35-1-7-deng-xiaoping-and-the-economic-reform/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"78\",\"title\":\"Forty years ago, Gorbachev took over – Why did socialism collapse?\",\"description\":\"Mar 11, 2025 · In the end, socialism collapsed because external shocks exposed and intensified the deep vulnerabilities of the socialist economies, which had ...\",\"url\":\"https://wiiw.ac.at/forty-years-ago-gorbachev-took-over--why-did-socialism-collapse-n-671.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"79\",\"title\":\"Venezuela: from socialist experiment to failed state | TheArticle\",\"description\":\"Aug 1, 2024 · They react as they have after every failed socialist experiment: They say, “That wasn't really socialism at all.” But next time, they promise, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thearticle.com/venezuela-from-socialist-experiment-to-failed-state\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"80\",\"title\":\"Why “Twenty-First-Century Socialism” Failed - Jacobin\",\"description\":\"Aug 4, 2016 · The failures of the much-touted “soci