est. countries in mid-1986, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/361600565_Understanding_the_Socialist-Market_Economy_in_Vietnam\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"91\",\"title\":\"Socialism and the market: China and Vietnam compared | Links\",\"description\":\"China's state sector decreased while its private sector grew, while Vietnam's state sector increased and its private sector grew less. China had more private ...\",\"url\":\"https://links.org.au/node/14\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"92\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The quest for the socialist market economy in China and Vietnam\",\"description\":\"This reformism begs reference to the old theoretical debates on \\\" market socialism \\\" and the narrow road out of State socialism with its mandatory fresh ...\",\"url\":\"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2021-08/010013516.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"93\",\"title\":\"The Horrors of Child Labor in Dickens' Time | Hartford Stage\",\"description\":\"Children were forced to work 12 to 16 hour days, living in overcrowded, filthy buildings on the factory property. By the beginning of the nineteenth century, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.hartfordstage.org/stagenotes/acc15/child-labor\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"94\",\"title\":\"Industrialization, Labor and Life - National Geographic Education\",\"description\":\"May 30, 2025 · Despite their important contributions, women and children received low pay for their labor. They were commonly forced to work 16 hours per day ...Missing:  facts | Show results with:facts\",\"url\":\"https://education.nationalgeographic.org/resource/industrialization-labor-and-life/7th-grade/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"95\",\"title\":\"1833 Factory Act - The National Archives\",\"description\":\"In 1833 the Government passed a Factory Act to improve conditions for children working in factories. Young children were working very long hours in workplaces.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/education/resources/1833-factory-act/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"96\",\"title\":\"Review: Proudhon's “What is Property?” | The Anarchist Library\",\"description\":\"The bulk of the book contains Proudhon's searing critique of property. This rests on two key concepts. Firstly, property allowed the owner to exploit its user.\",\"url\":\"https://theanarchistlibrary.org/library/anarcho-review-proudhon-s-what-is-property\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"97\",\"title\":\"Chapter V - What is Property? Proudhon 1840\",\"description\":\"Property is the suicide of society. Possession is a right; property is against right. Suppress property while maintaining possession, and, by this simple ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.marxists.org/reference/subject/economics/proudhon/property/ch05.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"98\",\"title\":\"Economic Manuscripts: Theories of Surplus-Value by Karl Marx 1863\",\"description\":\"Theories of Surplus-Value [Volume IV of Capital]. Written: 1863; Source: Theories of Surplus Value, Progress Publishers; Past Work: Julio Huato\",\"url\":\"https://www.marxists.org/archive/marx/works/1863/theories-surplus-value/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"99\",\"title\":\"The Multiple Meanings of Marx's Value Theory - Monthly Review\",\"description\":\"The vision of Marx's value theory as a theory of capitalist exploitation, tracing back surplus value to the extraction of living labor from human beings as ...\",\"url\":\"https://monthlyreview.org/articles/the-multiple-meanings-of-marxs-value-theory/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"100\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Marx's Value, Exchange and Surplus Value Theory\",\"description\":\"The principle of equivalence which rules in the market conceals it. Exploitation has then to be unveiled. However, Marx's theory is open to two main criticisms.\",\"url\":\"https://www.levyinstitute.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/wp26.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"101\",\"title\":\"Elements of Dialectical Ma