ique-utopian-socialists\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"107\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Marx's Critique of the Utopian Socialists Author(s)\",\"description\":\"failure of the Utopian socialists to realize their Utopian dreams: not only had they failed to transform society as a whole, but each of their demonstration.\",\"url\":\"https://www.cooperative-individualism.org/paden-roger_marx%27s-critique-of-the-utopian-socialists-2002.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"108\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Socialism: Utopian and Scientific - Marxists Internet Archive\",\"description\":\"In 1802, Saint-Simon's Geneva letters appeared; in. 1808 appeared Fourier's first work, although the groundwork of his theory dated from 1799; on January 1, ...Missing:  key | Show results with:key\",\"url\":\"https://www.marxists.org/archive/marx/works/download/Engels_Socialism_Utopian_and_Scientific.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"109\",\"title\":\"Socialism: utopian and scientific – an introduction - Counterfire\",\"description\":\"Jun 20, 2018 · Engels' popular pamphlet offers one of the best concise accounts of capitalist development and an accessible introduction to Marx's revolutionary socialism.\",\"url\":\"https://www.counterfire.org/article/socialism-utopian-and-scientific-an-introduction/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"110\",\"title\":\"The Dictatorship Of The Proletariat - Marxists Internet Archive\",\"description\":\"The dictatorship of the proletariat as new forms of the class struggle of the proletariat (in other words: its new stage and new tasks).\",\"url\":\"https://www.marxists.org/archive/lenin/works/1919/sep/x02.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"111\",\"title\":\"Section H - Why do anarchists oppose state socialism?\",\"description\":\"Yes. Anarchists have always argued that real socialism cannot be created using a state. The basic core of the argument is simple. Socialism implies equality, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.anarchistfaq.org/afaq/sectionH.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"112\",\"title\":\"What is Democratic Socialism? - Democratic Socialists of America\",\"description\":\"We believe that working people should run both the economy and society democratically to meet human needs, not to make profits for a few. Join Us Donate.Leadership and Structure · DSA Constitution \u0026 Bylaws · Socialist Forum\",\"url\":\"https://www.dsausa.org/about-us/what-is-democratic-socialism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"113\",\"title\":\"The role of the state and social democracy | The Communist\",\"description\":\"Sep 21, 2017 · Marxism teaches us that the state (that is to say, every state) is an instrument for the oppression of one class by another.\",\"url\":\"https://communist.red/the-role-of-the-state-and-social-democracy/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"114\",\"title\":\"The Soviets Tried to Run an Economy without Market Prices - FEE.org\",\"description\":\"The Soviet Union used a system of central planning called material balance planning, which balanced the total output of the economy with the total input.\",\"url\":\"https://fee.org/articles/the-soviets-tried-to-run-an-economy-without-market-prices/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"115\",\"title\":\"Mises on the Impossibility of Economic Calculation under Socialism\",\"description\":\"The problem of socialist economic calculation is precisely this: that in the absence of market prices for the factors of production, a computation of profit or ...\",\"url\":\"https://oll.libertyfund.org/pages/mises-on-the-impossibility-of-economic-calculation-under-socialism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"116\",\"title\":\"Hayek and the Impossibility of Socialist Calculation - J Edgar Mihelic\",\"description\":\"Mar 23, 2018 · Hayek notes that socialism and centrally planned systems arise when the worst actors forcibly come to power and thus end up on top.\",\"url\":\"https://mihelic.medium.com/hayek-and-the-impossibility-of-socialist-calculation-72037c106840\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"117\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Mises and Hayek on Calculation and Knowledge\",\"description\":\"\\\"While Mises saw calculation as the problem of socialism,\\\" says Jeffrey Herbener (1991, p. 43), \\\"Hayek views it as a knowledge problem.\\\" \\\"Mises demonstrated ...\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.mises.org/rae7_2_5_2.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"118\",\"title\":\"How Did the Soviet Economic System Affect Consumer Goods?\",\"description\":\"Sep 9, 2023 · Central planning made it difficult for administrators to respond to the country's shifting economic needs. Without market price signals, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.investopedia.com/ask/answers/050615/how-did-soviet-economic-system-affect-consumer-goods.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"119\",\"title\":\"Project Cybersyn: Chile's Radical Experiment in Cybernetic Socialism\",\"description\":\"Sep 11, 2023 · A military coup violently ended Chile's political experiment with socialism, and with it the nation's technological experiment with cybernetic management.\",\"url\":\"https://thereader.mitpress.mit.edu/project-cybersyn-chiles-radical-experiment-in-cybernetic-socialism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"120\",\"title\":\"Why Socialist Economies Fail | American Enterprise Institute - AEI\",\"description\":\"Dec 15, 2021 · Why Socialist Economies Fail ... Consider: Without competition and threat of failure, companies won't engage in game-changing innovation and the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.aei.org/economics/why-socialist-economies-fail/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"121\",\"title\":\"The knowledge problem – why central planning always fails\",\"description\":\"Mar 28, 2025 · One of the most fundamental reasons socialism and government intervention fail is what Austrian economist Friedrich Hayek called “the knowledge problem”.\",\"url\":\"https://freemarketfoundation.com/the-knowledge-problem-why-central-planning-always-fails/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"122\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Politics of Market Socialism - Harvard University\",\"description\":\"socialism: an economy in which firms are owned and controlled by the government but then sell their products to consumers in competi- tive markets. A ...\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.harvard.edu/files/shleifer/files/politics_market_socialism.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"123\",\"title\":\"The Forgotten Vision of Market Socialism\",\"description\":\"May 10, 2018 · 200 years after Marx's birth, a look at how two economists sought to reconcile his idea of common ownership with market mechanisms.\",\"url\":\"https://www.ineteconomics.org/perspectives/blog/the-forgotten-vision-of-market-socialism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"124\",\"title\":\"Economic Calculation in the Socialist Commonwealth - Mises Institute\",\"description\":\"This is the essay that overthrew the socialist paradigm in economics, and provided the foundation for modern Austrian price theory.\",\"url\":\"https://mises.org/library/book/economic-calculation-socialist-commonwealth\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"125\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Socialist Growth Revisited: Insights from Yugoslavia - LSE\",\"description\":\"Firms became labour-managed, or organized along the principles of self-management. Work councils, supposedly representing the interests of workers, could, in ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.lse.ac.uk/Economic-History/Assets/Documents/WorkingPapers/Economic-History/2017/WP268.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"126\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Phillips Curve in Self-management Socialism of Yugoslavia\",\"description\":\"Jul 29, 2022 · Abstract. Inflation and unemployment were two of the main issues that plagued the Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia.\",\"url\":\"https://mpra.ub.uni-muenchen.de/113920/1/MPRA_paper_113920.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"127\",\"title\":\"Theories in Market Socialism: Part I | by Aaron Medlin, PhD | Medium\",\"description\":\"Jul 3, 2018 · The historical cases generally defined as market socialist include Hungary, Yugoslavia, and China. Hungary oscillated between planning and ...\",\"url\":\"https://imedlinian.medium.com/theories-in-market-socialism-part-i-31a2866743cc\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"128\",\"title\":\"Yugoslav Self-Management and the Economics of Disaster\",\"description\":\"Aug 10, 2025 · The socialist Yugoslavia then developed a specific political system of workers' self-management, from 1950 (Liotta, 2001) . This political shift ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/30426362_Paradigm_Lost_Yugoslav_Self-Management_and_the_Economics_of_Disaster\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"129\",\"title\":\"Socialism and Incentives - FEE.org\",\"description\":\"Nov 1, 1986 · Critics often argue that because it “abolishes” profits and losses, socialism eliminates incentives. Defenders maintain that since it eliminates ...Missing:  critiques | Show results with:critiques\",\"url\":\"https://fee.org/articles/socialism-and-incentives/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"130\",\"title\":\"[PDF] A Democratic Enterprise-Based Market Socialism\",\"description\":\"Critics of pure self-managed market socialism have faulted it especially for inefficient capital formation and a bias toward consumption over investment ...\",\"url\":\"https://sites.lsa.umich.edu/tomweisskopf/wp-content/uploads/sites/278/2015/08/democratic-enterprise-based_market_socialism.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"131\",\"title\":\"Full article: Market socialism as a form of life - Taylor \u0026 Francis Online\",\"description\":\"1. Under market socialism, the political community owns capital and distributes its income in a democratically justified pattern.Missing:  performance | Show results with:performance\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00346764.2021.1886319\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"132\",\"title\":\"Reading: The Disadvantages of Socialism | International Business\",\"description\":\"Critics of socialism claims that it creates distorted or absent price signals, results in reduced incentives, causes reduced prosperity, has low feasibility, ...\",\"url\":\"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/suny-internationalbusiness/chapter/reading-the-disadvantages-of-socialism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"133\",\"title\":\"The Chronic Shortage Model of Centrally Planned Economies - jstor\",\"description\":\"The empirical evidence confirms the existence of chronic shortage. In each area further research would provide additional insights into the economics of. CPEs.Missing:  misallocation | Show results with:misallocation\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/152346\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"134\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Misallocations go a long way: evidence from firm-level data - GRAPE |\",\"description\":\"evidence on misallocation in centrally planned economies is ample, the actual empirical evidence is missing to the best of our knowledge. We bridge this gap ...\",\"url\":\"https://grape.org.pl/WP/31_HagemejerSzewczykTyrowicz_website.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"135\",\"title\":\"The Socialist Calculation Debate: Theory, History, and ...\",\"description\":\"Nov 29, 2024 · A century-long debate that was initiated by Ludwig von Mises in 1920. In so doing, it tells the history of the problem of economic calculation in the socialist ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.mercatus.org/hayekprogram/research/books/socialist-calculation-debate-theory-history-and-contemporary-relevance\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"136\",\"title\":\"Lenin: What Is To Be Done? - Marxists Internet Archive\",\"description\":\"Lenin's work What Is To Be Done? was written at the end of 1901 and early in 1902. In “Where To Begin”, published in Iskra, No. 4 (May 1901), Lenin said that ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.marxists.org/archive/lenin/works/1901/witbd/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"137\",\"title\":\"Lenin's game-changing concept of the vanguard party\",\"description\":\"The Bolshevik vanguard never declared itself the new state power. The Bolsheviks saw that workers, peasants, and soldiers were building soviets, their own ...\",\"url\":\"https://socialism.com/fs-article/lenins-game-changing-concept-of-the-vanguard-party/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"138\",\"title\":\"Democratic Centralism: Lenin's Organizational Principle\",\"description\":\"Feb 28, 2024 · Lenin's principle of democratic centralism combined democratic discussion and centralized decision-making within the Communist Party.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://polsci.institute/political-theory/democratic-centralism-lenin-organizational-principle/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"139\",\"title\":\"The Struggle for the Party, Chapter 8\",\"description\":\"By the Sixth Congress in late July, 240,000 persons belonged to the Bolshevik Party, and in the week before the October Revolution, Sverdlov told the Central ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.marxists.org/history/erol/ncm-2/loren/chapter8.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"140\",\"title\":\"The Dictatorship of the Proletariat - Marxists Internet Archive\",\"description\":\"The Bolsheviks, therefore, polled a little less than the Socialist-Revolutionaries. And so, by October-November 1917, the armed forces were half Bolshevik. If ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.marxists.org/archive/lenin/works/1919/dec/16.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"141\",\"title\":\"Constituent Assembly - Seventeen Moments in Soviet History\",\"description\":\"This decision bought the Bolsheviks valuable time, as many who were opposed to their seizure of power considered the Bolshevik government as another in a series ...\",\"url\":\"https://soviethistory.msu.edu/1917-2/constituent-assembly/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"142\",\"title\":\"Vladimir Lenin - (Intro to Political Science) - Fiveable\",\"description\":\"As the first leader of the Soviet Union, Vladimir Lenin established a system of one-party dictatorship and the suppression of political opposition, which laid ...\",\"url\":\"https://fiveable.me/key-terms/intro-to-poli-sci/vladimir-lenin\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"143\",\"title\":\"How Lenin's Red Terror set a macabre course for the Soviet Union\",\"description\":\"Sep 2, 2020 · Intent on maintaining their control of a country in the throes of a civil war, the Bolsheviks used terror tactics to silence their enemies and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/history/article/red-terror-set-macabre-course-soviet-union\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"144\",\"title\":\"100 Years of Communism—and 100 Million Dead | Hudson Institute\",\"description\":\"Nov 6, 2017 · ... Lenin ist ideology into reality. For the first time, a state was ... The victims include 200,000 killed during the Red Terror (1918-22); ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.hudson.org/national-security-defense/100-years-of-communism-and-100-million-dead\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"145\",\"title\":\"Authoritarian vs. Democratic Socialism: What's the Difference?\",\"description\":\"Oct 1, 2023 · Traditionally, socialism means government control of the means of production. This classic definition goes all the way back to Karl Marx and his Communist ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thecollector.com/democratic-socialism-authoritarian-socialism-difference/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"146\",\"title\":\"Don't confuse 'social democracy' and 'democratic socialism'\",\"description\":\"Sep 5, 2018 · Democratic socialism refers to the anti-capitalist philosophy that the public controls as the means of production through a planned economy.\",\"url\":\"https://dailyillini.com/opinions/2018/09/05/dont-confuse-social-democracy-and-democratic-socialism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"147\",\"title\":\"Social Democracy vs. Democratic Socialism: What's the Difference?\",\"description\":\"Jul 25, 2025 · Social Democracy: Reform the system to work better for everyone. Democratic Socialism: Transform the system to give ordinary people more power ...\",\"url\":\"https://goodparty.org/blog/article/social-democracy-vs-democratic-socialism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"148\",\"title\":\"Social Democracy Beats Democratic Socialism by Daron Acemoglu\",\"description\":\"Feb 17, 2020 · Democratic socialism has been conflated with social democracy. And, unfortunately, Sanders has contributed to this confusion.\",\"url\":\"https://www.project-syndicate.org/commentary/social-democracy-beats-democratic-socialism-by-daron-acemoglu-2020-02\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"149\",\"title\":\"The Making of Social Democracy: the Economic and Electoral ...\",\"description\":\"Abstract. Upon assuming power for the first time in 1935, the Norwegian Labour Party delivered on its promise for a major schooling reform. The reform rais.\",\"url\":\"https://academic.oup.com/jeea/article/23/1/119/7698112\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"150\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Making of Social Democracy | MIT Economics\",\"description\":\"Jan 25, 2024 · Upon assuming power for the first time in 1935, the Norwegian Labour Party delivered on its promise for a major schooling reform.\",\"url\":\"https://economics.mit.edu/sites/default/files/2024-01/The%2520Making%2520of%2520Social%2520Democracy.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"151\",\"title\":\"What is Modern Scandinavian Socialism in 2025? - Erik Examines\",\"description\":\"Jun 25, 2025 · Strictly speaking all Scandinavian countries have a capitalist economy, however many economists in Norway will characterize our economies as ...\",\"url\":\"https://erikexamines.substack.com/p/what-is-modern-scandinavian-socialism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"152\",\"title\":\"Capitalism and the Nordic Model - Scandinavian University Press\",\"description\":\"Mar 18, 2024 · Although seen as a 'tamedʼ form of capitalism, the Nordic model has never fully suspended capitalism as a historically distinctive mode of ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.scup.com/doi/10.18261/nwr.9.1.1\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"153\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://dissentmagazine.org/article/path-democratic-socialism-lessons