 · In tsarist Russia and interwar Poland, the Jewish Bund developed a socialist alternative to Zionism while fighting against antisemitic\",\"url\":\"https://jacobin.com/2022/06/jewish-labor-bund-nazi-genocide-wwii-labor-migration-anti-zionism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"176\",\"title\":\"The Bund by the Numbers: The Ebbs and Flows of a Jewish Radical ...\",\"description\":\"May 6, 2020 · The Bund is often portrayed as one of the largest political movements in Jewish Russia, so I was shocked to find that in 1910, the party had a mere 609 members.\",\"url\":\"https://ingeveb.org/blog/the-bund-by-the-numbers\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"177\",\"title\":\"The Socialism of Islam: Beyond \\\"Islamic Socialism\\\" - Hood Communist\",\"description\":\"Apr 25, 2024 · Mustafa Hosni Sibai (1915-64) was a Syrian Islamic thinker, considered to be one of the most important Islamic scholars of the twentieth ...\",\"url\":\"https://hoodcommunist.org/2024/04/25/the-socialism-of-islam-beyond-islamic-socialism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"178\",\"title\":\"Islamic Socialism: A history from left to right - World - DAWN.COM\",\"description\":\"Feb 21, 2013 · Its roots can be found amongst the works of Muslim thinkers and ideologues in South and East Asia, Africa and in various Middle Eastern (Arab) countries.\",\"url\":\"https://www.dawn.com/news/787645/islamic-socialism-a-history-from-left-to-right\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"179\",\"title\":\"Socialists and Islam | International Worker's League - LIT-CI\",\"description\":\"Sep 5, 2020 · The relationship of socialism in the 50s and 60s with Islam in the context of “anti-imperialism” was not limited to Algeria. Then there is the ...\",\"url\":\"https://litci.org/en/socialists-and-islam/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"180\",\"title\":\"T. H. Green and the Development of Ethical Socialism\",\"description\":\"This book uncovers the philosophical foundations of a tradition of ethical socialism best represented in the work of R.H. Taw